    "clinical": "<b>Fine Needle Aspiration Cytology (FNAC) in Clinical Practice.</b><br>In suspected animal tumours, FNAC using a 22-gauge needle and 5-ml syringe is the quickest, cheapest pre-operative test. For <b>CTVT</b> in dogs, an air-dried smear stained with Leishman's or Diff-Quik stain reveals round cells with characteristic multiple round clear cytoplasmic vacuoles (lipid-filled), providing a 100% definitive clinical diagnosis in 5 minutes without biopsy, directing treatment straight to <b>Vincristine sulphate (0.025 mg/kg IV weekly for 3-5 doses)</b>.",
