    "clinical": "<b>Emergency Lab Differentiation in Equine Colic vs Azoturia.</b><br>In a horse presenting with severe muscle stiffness, trembling, and reddish-brown urine: collect urine and blood immediately. Centrifuge both. If the horse has <b>Azoturia (Rhabdomyolysis / Monday Morning Disease)</b>, the urine supernatant is dark brown (myoglobinuria), but the <b>blood plasma is crystal clear</b> because myoglobin is small, has no plasma protein carrier, and clears the glomerulus immediately. If the plasma were pink, the horse would have intravascular haemolysis and haemoglobinuria.",
